{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfunv2c2P8oRitNBFEtmK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Technically yes, but it isn't the supported pattern and it often breaks.** An `Agent` is a Durable Object, so a stub from `env.MyAgent.get(env.MyAgent.newUniqueId())` can invoke its public methods over DO RPC. But the Agents SDK (built on partyserver) expects every instance to have a **name**, which it sets when you use `getAgentByName(env.MyAgent, \"some-name\")` or route through `routeAgentRequest`. With a raw unique ID, that name is never set. Anything that touches `this.name` will throw an error like \"Attempting to read .name … before it was set\", and that includes state sync, scheduling, MCP, and parts of initialization/`onStart`.\n\n**Recommendation:** use `getAgentByName()`. If you need a unique instance, generate an ID yourself (e.g. `crypto.randomUUID()`) and pass it as the name. RPC calls will then behave reliably."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2261,"cache_read_input_tokens":535,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2261},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8ff9024c-3ead-41b7-9d57-e612b1c6a56a","uuid":"85b6c971-c7ee-43d5-b056-2d571eac69b5","timestamp":"2026-10-11T04:08:34.761Z","request_id":"req_011Cfunv2Pdr9Z2ekSfnrgyq"}
